# 🏪 14. Real-World E-Commerce Data

Imagine an online shopping application.

A product could be represented as:

```javascript
let product = {
    id: 101,
    name: "Laptop",
    price: 55000,

    brand: {
        name: "Dell",
        country: "USA"
    },

    categories: [
        "Electronics",
        "Computers"
    ],

    stock: {
        available: true,
        quantity: 25
    }
};
```

### 🧠 Structure

```text
📦 Product
│
├── id
├── name
├── price
│
├── brand
│   ├── name
│   └── country
│
├── categories
│   ├── Electronics
│   └── Computers
│
└── stock
    ├── available
    └── quantity
```

Access the data:

```javascript
console.log(product.name);
console.log(product.brand.name);
console.log(product.categories[0]);
console.log(product.stock.quantity);
```

Output:

```text
Laptop
Dell
Electronics
25
```

